      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A search of the literature revealed that spontaneous coronary artery-left ventricular communications have only rarely been reported. These fistulae are frequently associated with angina pectoris which has been attributed to a ventricular steal phenomenon. The patient described herein presented with angina pectoris and was found to have multiple coronary arterioventricular communications without significant coronary atherosclerosis."},
